   "evidence": "The lemma it delegates to in the same PR does name the right-hand side: `TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Trace/FinTwo.lean:118` `pow_eq_neg_one_of_trace_eq_two_mul_cos_pi_div (htr : A.trace = 2 * cos (\u03c0 / k))`. Convention: \"to disambiguate the name of theorem or better convey the intended reference, it is necessary to describe some of the hypotheses\" \u2014 a dangling `_eq` conveys none. Mathlib's `_of_sq_eq` truncations (`IsPreconnected.eq_of_sq_eq`, Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/Field.lean:201) do not apply: there both sides are variables already bound in the name's context, here the right-hand side is a specific closed form.",
   "file": "TauCeti/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/ProjectiveSpecialLinearGroup/OrderOf.lean",
   "fix": "Spell out the right-hand side, e.g. `mk_pow_eq_one_of_trace_sq_eq_two_mul_cos_pi_div_sq`, matching the fully-named sibling it calls.",
   "issue": "`mk_pow_eq_one_of_trace_sq_eq` names a hypothesis (`trace A ^ 2 = (2 * cos (\u03c0 / k)) ^ 2`) but stops at `_eq`, so nothing in the name says what the squared trace equals \u2014 yet that right-hand side is what determines the `k` in the conclusion. A user searching for the `cos (\u03c0 / k)` trace criterion will not find it, and the name cannot be told apart from a hypothesis `trace A ^ 2 = 4` or `= 0`.",
   "line": 50
  }
